       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). The 1600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and they give no added benefit. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nHere are some options that fit common intents:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for this patient.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 400 mg every 6 hours for milder pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg/day**, which may have been intended as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm if the 1600 mg figure was deliberate. I'll enter the order once I have that. I can also add a note, such as \"take with food\"."
